    <briefdescription>
<para>Simple wrapper around std::function&lt;void(raw_ostream&amp;)&gt;. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class is useful to construct print helpers for <ref refid="classllvm_1_1raw__ostream" kindref="compound">raw_ostream</ref>.</para>
<para>Example: <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_printable" kindref="compound">Printable</ref> printRegister(unsigned Register) { return <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_printable" kindref="compound">Printable</ref>([<ref refid="classllvm_1_1_register" kindref="compound">Register</ref>](<ref refid="classllvm_1_1raw__ostream" kindref="compound">raw_ostream</ref> &amp;OS) { OS &lt;&lt; getRegisterName(Register); }); } ... OS &lt;&lt; printRegister(Register); ...</para>
<para>Implementation note: Ideally this would just be a typedef, but doing so leads to operator &lt;&lt; being ambiguous as function has matching constructors in some STL versions. I have seen the problem on gcc 4.6 libstdc++ and microsoft STL. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
